nodecode-dyscalculia is a rewrite of Dyscalculia-io's Dyscalculia-io/dyscalculia-agent-plugin:

  https://github.com/Dyscalculia-io/dyscalculia-agent-plugin
  commit a8083b1ba3667998025ed1bab15500ed8096ac35
  MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Dyscalculia.io (LICENSE)

Rewritten: the plugin was configuration only -- one hosted MCP server and one
skill -- so the rewrite speaks that same endpoint (https://mcp.dyscalculia.io/mcp)
from Lisp with the image's own HTTP call, and gives its six read-only tools as
six model tools in the DYSCALCULIA package, plus /dyscalculia and a manual
topic. The skill's guidance -- present a range across studies, cite the study
behind a figure, never state a figure the tools did not return, and the test is
a screening not a diagnosis -- is the primer (help :dyscalculia) answers.

Left out: the plugin's install and enable lines, which were Hermes's own, and
the Agent Skills packaging (`skills/dyscalculia-research/SKILL.md`, npx
`skills add`), which is the same text as the primer and would be a second copy
to keep in step. The server is spoken, not reimplemented, so the figures stay
the publisher's; the cell adds one thing the plugin did not have, a max_chars
bound on how much of an answer reaches the model.
